MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The flap discs fit the work suggested by my cutting wheels and metal drill bits: smoothing edges after cutting is a natural next step, provided the discs fit my equipment.",
    "The screws and brass rods fit my recurring fastening and fabrication work, while the foam could support cushioning and mounting tasks. Gloves also make sense for the messy adhesive and epoxy projects in my history, subject to material suitability."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The two filaments and UV printer resin require a printing setup I have not shown a need for. My tabletop epoxy was for a different process, so the shared resin wording does not make printer resin useful to me.",
    "Spray foam gun cleaner and the emergency switch serve specific tasks I do not currently have. Using adhesives and repair tools does not mean I have a foam dispensing gun or an electrical control project."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in making and repairing things seems to have been stretched into an interest in 3D printing, without a connection to the tools and supplies I actually use.",
    "Broad connections such as resin, adhesive, and workshop equipment seem to count too heavily when the recommended product serves a different purpose or needs additional equipment."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of screws, bolts, rivets, and rivet nuts show a sustained need for fastening and assembly supplies. A useful next choice should fill a size or application gap in those supplies.",
    "Compatibility and the next practical step matter to me: finishing a cut edge follows naturally from cutting metal, while buying specialized consumables only makes sense when I have the equipment and a current use for them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my hands-on repair and fabrication interests but stretched them into specialized activities that my history does not establish."
}
